        "type": "thinking",
        "thinking": "I'm checking the root जॄ in दिवादि, considering its present tense जीर्यति, and trying to recall whether it falls under the पुषादि group for the Luṅ (aorist) formation, referencing sutra 3.1.58 which lists जॄ among roots like स्तम्भ् and म्रुच् for a special aorist treatment.\n\nFor Luṅ, जॄ allows two forms under 3.1.58: अजरत् (अङ्-luṅ with गुण) or अजारीत् via सिच्. In madhyama-puruṣa bahuvacana, the अङ् form gives अजरत while the सिच् form gives अजारिष्ट, since 7.2.40 blocks दीर्घ in सिच् परस्मैपद but वृद्धि still applies. I'm also noting that झॄ, a separate root meaning the same thing, isn't listed in 3.1.58, so it only takes सिच् forms like अझारीत्, अझारिष्टाम्, अझारिषुः, and the corresponding मध्यमपुरुष/उत्तमपुरुष forms.\n\n",
